🌳 TreeMap vs HashMap in Java (Focus: Ordering)

| Feature                  | **HashMap**                                             | **TreeMap**                                    |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| **Ordering**             | ❌ **No ordering** — keys are **unsorted** and unordered | ✅ **Sorted by keys** (natural or custom order) |
| **Underlying Structure** | Hash table (buckets via hashCode)                       | Red-Black Tree (balanced BST)                  |
| **Null Keys**            | ✅ Allows **one null key**                               | ❌ Does **not allow null keys**                 |
| **Performance**          | 🔁 Faster (`O(1)` for get/put)                          | ⏳ Slower (`O(log n)` for get/put)              |
| **Use Case**             | When order doesn’t matter, and speed is priority        | When **sorted key order** is required          |
| **Thread-safe?**         | ❌ No                                                    | ❌ No                                           |
| **Implements**           | `Map` interface                                         | `NavigableMap` (extends `SortedMap`)           |


✅ Example: HashMap (No Order)
java
Copy
Edit
Map<String, Integer> hashMap = new HashMap<>();
hashMap.put("Banana", 1);
hashMap.put("Apple", 2);
hashMap.put("Mango", 3);

System.out.println(hashMap);
// Output: Random order like {Mango=3, Apple=2, Banana=1}
✅ Example: TreeMap (Sorted by Keys)
java
Copy
Edit
Map<String, Integer> treeMap = new TreeMap<>();
treeMap.put("Banana", 1);
treeMap.put("Apple", 2);
treeMap.put("Mango", 3);

System.out.println(treeMap);
// Output: Sorted by key: {Apple=2, Banana=1, Mango=3}
🧠 Key Point:
Use HashMap for fast access, no need for order.

Use TreeMap when you need sorted keys or range-based operations (e.g., subMap, headMap, tailMap).

⚠️ Important Notes:
TreeMap can use a custom Comparator for sorting.

TreeMap is useful when implementing navigation-based maps like:

java
Copy
Edit
treeMap.lowerKey("Mango");  // Gives the key just less than Mango

🎯 Summary
| Use **HashMap** When...        | Use **TreeMap** When...                  |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |
| You need **fast performance**  | You need **sorted keys**                 |
| You don’t care about key order | You want keys in natural or custom order |
| Null keys are acceptable       | Null keys must be avoided                |
